## 2. System design

### 2.1 Architecture

```
Browser (HTML + vanilla JS, self-hosted font, no CDN)
   │  form POST (auth, account)        fetch JSON (/api/*) + X-CSRF-Token header
   ▼
Flask app (app/__init__.py: create_app, security headers, CSRF hook, error handlers)
   auth blueprint        views blueprint         api blueprint
   (register/login/      (dashboard/account/     (health/predictions/checkins/
    logout)               export)                 venues/accuracy)
        │                      │                        │
        └──── services/repository.py: every SQL statement, scoped by session user_id ───┐
                       services/prediction_service.py ─────────────┐                   │
                                                                    ▼                   ▼
                               predictor/algorithm.py (pure Python)          SQLite: instance/syncromove.db
                                                                               users, venues, checkins,
                                                                               predictions, login_attempts,
                                                                               app_meta

One-off setup:  python scripts/import_dataset.py --data <NYC file>
                  → data/venues.csv.gz                     (venue list + popularity, committed)
                  → data/samples/sample_histories.json.gz  (25 real dataset users, committed)
                python scripts/generate_synthetic.py
                  → data/samples/synthetic_histories.json.gz (25 made-up past-year histories, the default)
Measuring:      python scripts/evaluate.py --data <NYC file> → docs/evaluation_results.json, docs/accuracy.png
Docs:           python scripts/render_docs.py → docs/LLD.md, docs/EVALUATION.md (figures filled from the JSON)
```

The **same** functions in `predictor/algorithm.py` serve the app and the evaluation script
(`compute_signals`, `weighted_totals`, the shared `rank_key` ordering), so the measured accuracy is
the accuracy of the code users get. A unit test checks that the app's `combine()` and the
evaluator's `weighted_totals()` give identical scores.

**Stack.** Python 3.11+, Flask 3.x, SQLite (stdlib `sqlite3`), werkzeug password hashing (scrypt),
waitress for serving, pytest. Data files use stdlib `csv`, `gzip` and `json`: no pandas, numpy or ML
libraries. No ORM, no front-end framework, no external CDN or font service. matplotlib is a
development dependency, used only for the evaluation chart.

### 2.2 Low level design

#### Client-side validation (`app/static/js/validate.js`, `dashboard.js`)
| Form | Rules and messages |
|---|---|
| Register | Email required, valid format, ≤ 254 chars ("Enter a valid email address, like name@example.com."); password ≥ 8 chars with a letter and a number ("Password needs at least one number."); confirm must match ("Passwords don't match."). The message appears under the field, the field gets `aria-invalid`, and the submit is blocked |
| Login | Both fields required |
| Check-in | A place must be selected from the search results ("Choose a place from the search results."); time required, not in the future, not earlier than the last check-in shown |
| Prediction time picker | Must be a valid date-time ("Enter a valid date and time.") |
| Account deletes | Password required |

HTML5 attributes (`required`, `maxlength`, `type=email`) are present for semantics. Forms use
`novalidate` so the JS module shows consistent plain-language messages.

#### Server-side validation (`app/validators.py`)
Every client rule is repeated on the server, plus what the browser can't check:

| Rule | Status, code |
|---|---|
| Email not already registered (case-insensitive, `COLLATE NOCASE`) | 409 |
| Venue id is 24 hex chars | 400 |
| Venue exists | 404 `not_found` |
| Venue differs from the user's last check-in ("You're already checked in here.") | 409 `duplicate` |
| Timestamp is ISO 8601 **with offset** | 400 |
| Timestamp not > 5 min in the future | 400 |
| Timestamp not before the last check-in | 409 `out_of_order` |
| `tz_offset_min` (and `tz`) in −720..840 | 400 |
| `k` in 1..10 | 400 |
| Search text 1..60 chars; LIKE wildcards escaped | 400 |
| JSON body is an object | 400 |
| Body ≤ 32 KB (`MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH`) | 413 |
| CSRF token on every POST (form field or `X-CSRF-Token`) | 403 `csrf_failed` |
| Login rate limit: 5 failures per email **or** IP in 15 min ("Too many failed attempts. Try again in N minutes.") | 429 |
| Wrong email or password (same message for both) | 401 |

API errors always have the shape `{"error": {"code", "field", "message"}}`.

