Pages (server-rendered): `GET/POST /register`, `GET/POST /login`, `POST /logout`, `GET /dashboard`,
`GET/POST /account` (delete check-ins or the account; password re-entry required),
`GET /account/export` (JSON download of all the user's data).

JSON API (session cookie; POSTs need `X-CSRF-Token`; every response `Cache-Control: no-store`):

| Endpoint | Request | Response |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /api/health` | — | `{"status":"ok","venues_loaded":38333,"algorithm_version":"rule-v1"}`; `"degraded"` + `message` if the venues file is missing. No auth |
| `GET /api/predictions` | `?k=3&tz=330&at=<ISO 8601, optional>` | `{algorithm_version, cold_start, history_used, query_ts_utc, time_bucket:"weekday 18:00-21:00", weights, last_place:{venue_id,category,lat,lon}, predictions:[{rank, venue_id, category, lat, lon, probability, score, distance_km, reason_code, reason, signals:{transition,time,frequency,recency,popularity}}]}` |
| `GET /api/checkins` | `?limit=10` (1..100) | `{checkins:[{checkin_id, venue_id, category, lat, lon, ts_utc, tz_offset_min, source, predicted_rank}], stats:{total, own, scored, hits_top3}}` |
| `POST /api/checkins` | `{"venue_id":"<24 hex>","timestamp":"<ISO 8601>"\|null,"tz_offset_min":330}` | `201 {checkin_id, venue_id, category, ts_utc, predicted_rank}`; `predicted_rank` = rank in the last prediction shown for the current place (1–3 hit, 0 miss, null if none shown) |
| `GET /api/venues` | `?q=coffee&limit=12` (1..50) | `{venues:[{venue_id, category, lat, lon, popularity, distance_km}], near_last_checkin}`: category search, nearest first (most popular first for a user with no check-ins) |
| `GET /api/accuracy` | — | Summary of `evaluation_results.json` plus `you: {total, own, scored, hits_top3}` |

**Data files.** `venues.csv.gz`: `venue_id,category,latitude,longitude,popularity`.
`sample_histories.json.gz`: `{dataset_user_id: [[venue_id, ts_utc, tz_offset_min], …]}`.

**Raw dataset.** 8 columns by position: user id, venue id, category id, category name, latitude,
longitude, timezone offset (minutes), UTC time (`Tue Apr 03 18:00:09 +0000 2012`). The original is
tab-separated with no header; a Kaggle CSV copy with a header also works. The file is **not valid
UTF-8** (byte 0xE9 in "Café"), so the reader tries UTF-8 and falls back to latin-1.

### 2.3 UI
A transit map, because the subject is moving through a city:

- **Hero:** the user's last 8 check-ins as a thick teal subway line between station dots, plotted
  at their real coordinates. It uses an equirectangular projection scaled by cos(latitude) in a
  padded bounding box, inline SVG, no map tiles, and a scale bar. The last stop is marked "You are
  here". The three predictions branch off as dashed lines in amber `#E3A008`, green `#23935F` and
  violet `#6E4FC4`, ending in numbered "subway bullets". Bullets closer than about 46 px to the
  current stop are pushed outward, and labels are placed with a small collision check so nearby
  places stay readable.
- **Next stops:** a numbered bullet, category, reason, distance and likelihood bar for each place.
  "Why?" opens a table of the four signal values × weights = contribution, with the winning signal
  in bold.
- **Panels:** Check in (category search → nearest places → time → button), Recent visits (tags
  "Predicted #2" / "Missed" / "Sample"), How accurate is this? (top-1/3/5, baseline comparison,
  the user's own top-3 hit rate).
- Palette: paper `#E9EEF1`, ink `#17212B`, muted `#5B6875`, teal `#0F6E8C`, error `#B42318`.
  Overpass (self-hosted variable woff2, SIL OFL), tabular figures.
- CSP `default-src 'self'`: no inline scripts or style attributes. Works at 360 px wide (taller
  map frame and larger map text on narrow screens), visible focus rings, `prefers-reduced-motion`
  respected, plain sentence-case copy, and empty states that say what to do.

