## 3. Data design

### 3.1 Tables (SQLite, `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON`)
| Table | Columns |
|---|---|
| `users` | `user_id INTEGER PK AUTOINCREMENT`, `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE COLLATE NOCASE`, `password_hash TEXT NOT NULL`, `created_at TEXT NOT NULL`, `sample_source TEXT NULL` |
| `venues` | `venue_id TEXT PK`, `category TEXT NOT NULL`, `latitude REAL NOT NULL`, `longitude REAL NOT NULL`, `popularity INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0`, `name TEXT NULL`, `owner_user_id INTEGER NULL FK→users ON DELETE CASCADE`; indexes on `category`, `owner_user_id`. Dataset venues have no owner; a place found from a user's detected location (`POST /api/places/locate`, OpenStreetMap lookup) belongs to that user and is never shown to anyone else. Older databases get the two columns added on start |
| `checkins` | `checkin_id INTEGER PK`, `user_id INTEGER FK→users ON DELETE CASCADE`, `venue_id TEXT FK→venues`, `ts_utc INTEGER NOT NULL`, `tz_offset_min INTEGER NOT NULL`, `source TEXT CHECK IN ('app','sample')`, `predicted_rank INTEGER NULL`, `created_at TEXT`; index `(user_id, ts_utc)` |
| `predictions` | `prediction_id INTEGER PK`, `user_id FK ON DELETE CASCADE`, `batch_id TEXT`, `context_checkin_id INTEGER FK→checkins ON DELETE CASCADE`, `rank INTEGER`, `venue_id TEXT FK`, `score REAL`, `algorithm_version TEXT`, `created_at TEXT`; index `(user_id, prediction_id)`. A batch identical to the previous one for the same context is not logged again |
| `login_attempts` | `attempt_id PK`, `email TEXT COLLATE NOCASE`, `ip TEXT`, `attempted_at INTEGER`; indexes `(email, attempted_at)`, `(ip, attempted_at)` |
| `app_meta` | `key TEXT PK`, `value TEXT` (sha-256 of the loaded venues file) |

### 3.2 Access levels
| Table | Anonymous | Logged-in user | Prediction service | Import script (host) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| users | insert (register) | read/delete **own row**; `password_hash` read only by login and password re-entry | — | — |
| venues | — | read | read | insert/update (via the venue file, synced on start) |
| checkins | — | read/insert/delete **own** | read the session user's rows | — |
| predictions | — | read own (export) | **insert only** | — |
| login_attempts | written by the login route | — | — | — |

Enforced in code: every repository function takes the session `user_id`, and no endpoint
accepts a user id from the client. A test checks that user B sees none of user A's check-ins.

### 3.3 Design considerations
- **Missing values and duplicates:** the file has no nulls; 250 exact duplicate rows are dropped
  ({{int:dataset.rows_raw}} → {{int:dataset.rows_after_dedup}}). Venues have no names, so the UI shows
  category, distance and coordinates. Coordinates vary slightly between check-ins of the same
  venue, so the median is used; the category is the most frequent label.
- **Indexes:** `(user_id, ts_utc)` for reading history; `category` for search;
  `(user_id, prediction_id)` for the latest batch; `(email|ip, attempted_at)` for the rate limit.
- **Size:** {{int:dataset.rows_raw}} rows (31.5 MB raw), 38,333 venues (0.8 MB gzipped). A sample history
  copies about 300–600 rows. Reading 1,000 check-ins and scoring the candidates takes milliseconds;
  the venue table (38k rows) is cached in memory per process; nothing else is cached.
- **Privacy:** location history is personal data. Passwords are hashed with werkzeug scrypt.
  Sessions are HttpOnly + SameSite=Lax, signed with a per-install secret, 12 h lifetime, and
  cleared and re-issued on login. CSRF protects every POST. Headers: CSP, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`,
  `nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, `Cache-Control: no-store` on pages and API. SQL is
  parameterised only. Users can export and delete all their data, `ON DELETE CASCADE` removes
  everything with the account, and the browser makes no third-party requests.

