## 5. Evaluation (measuring, not training)

Full detail in [EVALUATION.md](EVALUATION.md).

### 5.1 Protocol
All de-duplicated check-ins are sorted by time; the last {{pct:dataset.test_fraction}} (from {{raw:dataset.cutoff_utc}} UTC) are the
test window. City popularity is counted only from earlier check-ins. For each test check-in with an
earlier check-in, the profile holds **only that user's earlier check-ins**; the query time is the
real check-in time; we record the rank of the place actually visited (a miss if never visited
before). Nothing from the future is used.

### 5.2 Results ({{int:dataset.test_checkins}} test check-ins, every one counted)
| Method | Top-1 | Top-3 | Top-5 | MRR |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| City popularity only | {{pct:methods.popularity.top1}} | {{pct:methods.popularity.top3}} | {{pct:methods.popularity.top5}} | {{num3:methods.popularity.mrr}} |
| Baseline: user's most visited | {{pct:methods.most_visited.top1}} | {{pct:methods.most_visited.top3}} | {{pct:methods.most_visited.top5}} | {{num3:methods.most_visited.mrr}} |
| Markov only (order 1, back-off to frequency) | {{pct:methods.markov.top1}} | {{pct:methods.markov.top3}} | {{pct:methods.markov.top5}} | {{num3:methods.markov.mrr}} |
| SyncroMove, `W_TIME = 0` | {{pct:methods.full_no_time.top1}} | {{pct:methods.full_no_time.top3}} | {{pct:methods.full_no_time.top5}} | {{num3:methods.full_no_time.mrr}} |
| **SyncroMove (§4.3)** | **{{pct:methods.full.top1}}** | **{{pct:methods.full.top3}}** | **{{pct:methods.full.top5}}** | **{{num3:methods.full.mrr}}** |

Full rule extras: right category in the top 3 categories {{pct:full_extras.top3_category}}; a top-3 place within 1 km of
the real one {{pct:full_extras.top3_within_1km}}; top-3 by earlier history {{pct:full_extras.top3_by_history.<50.top3}} (< 50), {{pct:full_extras.top3_by_history.50-199.top3}} (50–199),
{{pct:full_extras.top3_by_history.200+.top3}} (200+); per-user median top-3 {{pct:full_extras.per_user_median_top3}}.

All top-1/3/5 figures are within ±1 point of the spec's reference run (most within 0.1).
[EVALUATION.md](EVALUATION.md#comparison-with-the-specs-reference-run-52) lists the small known
differences: the cutoff minute, 2 test check-ins, and the popularity-only MRR.

### 5.3 Accuracy expectation
Predicting the exact venue out of tens of thousands is hard. **{{pct:methods.full.top3}} top-3 with no training** is a
solid result on this data and beats the most-visited baseline by {{pt:methods.full.top3-methods.most_visited.top3}} points. Two things cap it:
{{pct:full_extras.never_visited_before}} of test check-ins are at places the user had never been before, which no
history-based ranker can predict; and knowing the time of day is worth {{pt:methods.full.top3-methods.full_no_time.top3}} points by itself. We do not
claim 90%+. Where a higher headline is useful, the category-level ({{pct:full_extras.top3_category}}) and within-1 km
({{pct:full_extras.top3_within_1km}}) figures are reported, labelled as such.

